            <ArticleTitle>Outpatient management of survivors of acute coronary syndromes.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>12-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>More patients are both suffering and surviving acute coronary syndromes. After hospital discharge, a host of interventions, including medications, therapeutic lifestyle changes, revascularization, and electrophysiologic devices improve quality of life and survival. Evidence-based management requires the general internist to have a working knowledge of these interventions and to identify patients whose outcomes would benefit from subspecialty referral.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
